# Playwright: captured PNGs for human review, test artifacts (traces/failure
# screenshots), and the HTML report. All are rebuilt from scratch on every run so
# committing them would just be stale bytes.
# The screenshot BASELINES under tests/e2e/*-snapshots/ are NOT ignored: those are the
# comparison targets and must be versioned.
#
# NOTE: the seeded DATA sandbox (auth token + metrics DB + event store) no longer lives
# under the repo at all — tests/e2e/seed.js puts it at
# <validated-temp-root>/cheaper-e2e-<uid>-<checkout-hash>, specifically so a repo-scoped
# `git clean` or a deploy automation walking this tree can never touch it. The checkout
# hash keeps concurrent worktrees from wiping each other's live run.
#
# There is intentionally NO ignore rule for it here, and adding one would be a mistake:
# seed.js hard-rejects any sandbox path that resolves inside this repo (that is how a
# hostile TMPDIR of "." is caught), so a `cheaper-e2e-*` directory showing up in
# `git status` means a guard has failed and must be seen, not hidden.
.playwright-artifacts/
.playwright-shots/
.playwright-report/
test-results/

# Throwaway git fixtures created by scripts/test-deploy-preflight.sh. They are real
# repos with their own bare remotes, and while the test runs they would otherwise show
# up as untracked work in THIS repo — which the deploy pre-flight (correctly) refuses on.
scripts/.preflight-testws/
scripts/.preflight-pusher/
